<title>Explore local mode shares · Microcensus & MATSim</title><style>__LEAFLET_CSS__
__DRAW_CSS__</style><style>
[hidden]{display:none!important}:root{--ink:#182b45;--blue:#176b94;--rose:#dc5675;--soft:#edf3f8;--muted:#53677e}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f1f5f9;color:var(--ink);font:15px system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}header{padding:24px 30px;background:#132c47;color:white}header h1{margin:5px 0;font-size:27px;letter-spacing:-.5px}header p{margin:8px 0 0;max-width:1000px;color:#d4e2ef}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#9eddeb}.layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(360px,1fr) minmax(460px,1fr);gap:18px;padding:20px;max-width:1800px;margin:auto}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #dce5ef;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 3px 15px #13305209;overflow:hidden}.controls{padding:18px;display:grid;gap:12px}label{font-weight:600;display:block;font-size:13px}select,input,button{font:inherit;border:1px solid #becddd;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 11px;background:white;color:var(--ink)}button{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}button:hover{background:#e9f2f8}button.primary{background:var(--blue);color:white;border-color:var(--blue)}.row{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap}.row label{flex:1;min-width:75px}.row input,.row select{width:100%;margin-top:5px}#map{height:570px;background:#e9eef2}.map-note{padding:10px 16px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.selection{font-size:13px;padding:10px;background:var(--soft);border-radius:8px}.results{padding:22px}.results h2{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:21px}.muted{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;line-height:1.5}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin:20px 0}.stat{padding:16px;background:var(--soft);border-radius:10px;border-top:3px solid var(--blue)}.stat.sim{border-color:var(--rose)}.stat b{font-size:30px;display:block;letter-spacing:-1px}.stat small{display:block;margin-top:4px;color:var(--muted)}#chart{width:100%;min-height:260px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{padding:10px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #e5edf4;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}thead{background:var(--soft)}.legend{display:flex;gap:20px;font-size:13px;margin:10px 0}.dot{display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;margin-right:6px;border-radius:3px}#status{font-weight:600}details{margin-top:18px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.empty{padding:30px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted)}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:wait}.warning{color:#96530c;background:#fff4df;padding:9px;border-radius:7px;margin:10px 0;font-size:12px}a{color:#146a94}@media(max-width:1000px){.layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:12px}#map{height:420px}header{padding:20px}}
</style></head><body>
<header><div class="eyebrow">Spatial demand diagnostics</div><h1>Explore local mode shares</h1><p>Compare Microcensus and MATSim for an area you choose. Draw a polygon, place a circle, or click a municipality or canton. Survey trips retain their person weights.</p></header>
<main class="layout"><section class="card"><div class="controls">
<div class="row"><button id="drawPolygon" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Draw polygon</button><button id="pickCentre" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Circle</button><button id="municipalityMode" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Municipality</button><button id="cantonMode" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Canton</button><button id="national" disabled>All filtered trips</button></div>
<div class="row" id="circleControls" hidden><label>Latitude<input id="latitude" type="number" step="any" value="47.3781762"></label><label>Longitude<input id="longitude" type="number" step="any" value="8.54021154"></label><label>Radius (m)<input id="radius" type="number" min="1" max="300000" step="100" value="2000"></label><button id="applyCircle" disabled>Use circle</button></div>
<div class="row" id="municipalityControls" hidden><label>Municipality<input id="municipalitySearch" type="search" placeholder="Search name or BFS number"></label><label>Select municipality<select id="municipality"><option value="">Choose…</option></select></label></div>
<div class="row" id="cantonControls" hidden><label>Select canton<select id="canton"><option value="">Choose…</option></select></label></div>
<div class="row"><label>Map opacity<input id="opacity" type="range" min="0" max="1" value="0.7" step="0.05"></label></div>
<div class="row"><label>Trips included<select id="direction"><option value="arrivals">Arrivals · destination inside</option><option value="departures">Departures · origin inside</option><option value="either">Origin OR destination inside</option><option value="both">Origin AND destination inside</option><option value="residents">Residents · home inside</option></select></label></div>
<div class="selection" id="selection">All filtered trips · no geographical restriction</div></div><div id="map" aria-label="Map for spatial selection"></div>
<div class="map-note" id="mapNote">Map: © swisstopo, geo.admin.ch. Geometry selection and results remain usable if background tiles cannot load.</div></section>
<section class="card results"><h2>Microcensus vs MATSim</h2><div class="row" role="group" aria-label="Results view" style="margin:14px 0"><button id="modeShareView" class="primary" aria-pressed="true">Mode shares</button><button id="distanceView" aria-pressed="false">Distances</button></div><p id="viewExplanation" class="muted">Weighted survey trip shares compared with simulated trip shares.</p><div id="status" class="muted" role="status">Loading embedded trip data…</div>
<div class="cards"><div class="stat"><span id="surveyMetricLabel">Microcensus observations</span><b id="surveyTrips">—</b><small id="surveySample"></small><small id="surveyPeople">— respondents with selected trips</small><small id="surveyWeight">— weighted trips</small></div><div class="stat sim"><span id="simMetricLabel">MATSim simulated trips</span><b id="simTrips">—</b><small id="simSample"></small><small id="simPeople">— simulated people with selected trips</small><small>Counts refer to this simulation sample.</small></div></div>
<div class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:#176b94"></i>Microcensus</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#dc5675"></i>MATSim</span></div>
<div id="chart"></div><div style="overflow-x:auto"><table><thead><tr id="numberHeaders"><th>Mode</th><th>Mz share</th><th>MATSim share</th><th>Difference</th><th>Mz trips</th><th>Sim. trips</th></tr></thead><tbody id="numbers"></tbody></table></div>
<div id="smallSample"></div><div class="row" style="margin-top:15px"><button id="download" disabled>Download selected statistics CSV</button></div>
<details><summary>How are these numbers calculated?</summary><p>Each row is one trip retained by the existing ModeShareAnalyzer. Microcensus shares sum person_weight across the selected trips of each mode and divide by the selected total trip weight. MATSim trips each have weight one. The observation counts are raw, unweighted trips; people are distinct respondents or simulated agents represented by those trips. People without retained trips do not appear in these counts.</p>
<p>The survey keeps its existing weekday, diary-quality, mode, distance and Swiss-geography filters. MATSim keeps its existing person, mode, distance and destination-purpose filters; trips with an airport activity at either endpoint are excluded before all summaries. This map uses the same domestic-resident cohort as the global mode-share figures. This is a comparison of shares, not a comparison of expanded population trip totals.</p>
<p>Residents means all retained trips by people whose home is in the selected area, including their trips outside it. Either endpoint counts each trip only once. Both endpoints requires both to be inside. Shapes include their boundaries. Municipality and canton selections use their original boundary geometry. Choose their buttons to show clickable boundaries. Circles use great-circle distance from the chosen point. Coordinates are stored at microdegree precision (roughly 0.1 m); results at an exact boundary may be affected by rounding.</p><p id="locationCoverage"></p>
<p>The distance view uses each retained trip’s Euclidean distance, in kilometres, from the same analyzer data. Means and quantiles use person_weight for Microcensus and weight one for MATSim. The all-modes row pools trips directly; it does not average the mode-specific means. Boxes span the 25th to 75th percentiles, the line is the median, whiskers show the 10th and 90th percentiles, and diamonds mark the mean. Quantiles use the inverse weighted empirical distribution: the first observed distance whose cumulative weight reaches the requested fraction. Nonfinite or negative distances are omitted only from distance summaries; valid-distance counts are shown and exported. The mode-share denominator is unchanged.</p>
<p>Only the map background needs internet access. Trip records, municipality and canton boundaries, controls and statistics are embedded in this file. This page requires a modern browser with Web Workers and DecompressionStream support.</p></details>
</section></main>
